CAT = "mypceRegulation"; SEG = "REG"
Q = [
("Which body regulates and supervises insurers in Malaysia?",
 "Bank Negara Malaysia", ["Securities Commission Malaysia", "Companies Commission of Malaysia", "Ministry of Domestic Trade"],
 "Bank Negara Malaysia (BNM) regulates insurers, takaful operators, brokers and adjusters under the Financial Services Act 2013 and the Islamic Financial Services Act 2013."),
("Which law governs conventional insurance business in Malaysia?",
 "Financial Services Act 2013", ["Islamic Financial Services Act 2013", "Capital Markets and Services Act 2007", "Companies Act 2016"],
 "The FSA 2013 governs conventional insurers and replaced the Insurance Act 1996. Takaful is governed by the Islamic Financial Services Act 2013."),
("Takaful operators in Malaysia are governed mainly by the:",
 "Islamic Financial Services Act 2013", ["Financial Services Act 2013", "Capital Markets and Services Act 2007", "Consumer Protection Act 1999"],
 "The IFSA 2013 regulates takaful operators, which must also follow Shariah requirements."),
("If a member insurer fails, policy owners are protected up to set limits by:",
 "PIDM", ["LIAM", "OFS", "PIAM"],
 "Perbadanan Insurans Deposit Malaysia runs the Takaful and Insurance Benefits Protection System, which protects eligible benefits if a member insurer fails."),
("A claimant unhappy with an insurer's final decision on a claim may refer the dispute, free, to the:",
 "Ombudsman for Financial Services", ["Securities Commission Malaysia", "Magistrates' Court registry", "Life Insurance Association of Malaysia"],
 "The Ombudsman for Financial Services (OFS) resolves disputes between consumers and its member financial service providers after the provider's own complaints process."),
("Before a life agent may sell, the agent must be registered with:",
 "LIAM", ["PIAM", "PIDM", "OFS"],
 "Life agents are registered with the Life Insurance Association of Malaysia (LIAM) through the industry's agency registration system; general agents register through PIAM."),
("General insurance agents in Malaysia are registered with:",
 "PIAM", ["LIAM", "PIDM", "MTA"],
 "The General Insurance Association of Malaysia (PIAM) keeps the register of general insurance agents. MTA is the takaful association."),
("An insurance broker in Malaysia acts on behalf of:",
 "The client", ["The insurer", "Bank Negara", "The loss adjuster"],
 "A broker is the client's representative, arranging cover with insurers. An agent represents the insurer that appointed him."),
("A client pays a large single premium in cash and asks for the policy to be cancelled soon after. An agent should:",
 "Report it as a suspicious transaction", ["Refund the cash to a friend's account", "Warn the client about the report", "Ignore it if the client is polite"],
 "Under the AMLA, unusual transactions are reported to the insurer's compliance officer, who reports to Bank Negara's financial intelligence unit."),
("Under the AMLA, telling a client that a suspicious transaction report has been made is:",
 "Tipping off, an offence", ["Required by good faith", "Allowed after a month", "Allowed if the client asks"],
 "Tipping off a customer about a suspicious transaction report or investigation is a criminal offence under the Anti-Money Laundering, Anti-Terrorism Financing and Proceeds of Unlawful Activities Act 2001."),
("Checking a new client's identity documents before issuing a policy is part of:",
 "Customer due diligence", ["Proximate cause review", "Claims settlement", "Premium rate setting"],
 "Insurers must identify and verify customers and beneficial owners under BNM's anti-money laundering requirements."),
("Under the Personal Data Protection Act 2010, an agent who collects a client's data must:",
 "Tell the client the purpose", ["Sell it to other agents", "Keep it for as long as she likes", "Share it on social media"],
 "The notice and choice principle requires a written notice telling the person why their data is collected and to whom it may be disclosed."),
("Which is one of the personal data protection principles in the PDPA 2010?",
 "The security principle", ["The indemnity principle", "The subrogation principle", "The average principle"],
 "The PDPA principles include general, notice and choice, disclosure, security, retention, data integrity and access."),
("An agent tells a client that a policy offers returns it does not offer. Under the FSA this is:",
 "Prohibited business conduct", ["Acceptable sales puffery", "A minor administrative slip", "Only an internal company matter"],
 "Schedule 7 of the FSA prohibits misleading or deceptive conduct, including misrepresenting the terms or benefits of a policy."),
("Requiring a borrower to buy a policy from one named insurer as a condition of a loan is:",
 "Prohibited as undue pressure", ["Required under the FSA 2013", "A normal cross-selling method", "Allowed for any housing loan"],
 "Schedule 7 of the FSA prohibits exerting undue pressure or coercion, including forcing a consumer to buy a product as a condition of another."),
("A loss adjuster is a specialist who:",
 "Assesses claims for insurers", ["Sells policies to the public", "Sets the motor premium tariff", "Decides consumer complaints"],
 "Loss adjusters, usually appointed by the insurer, investigate the cause and size of a loss and recommend a settlement."),
]
